+# Jace Teams-after-Singles diagnostic — Slippi 3.7.0
+
+This source/update kit tests **one connected singles game plus one Teams search**
+using one account and one Dolphin window. GitHub's Windows runner builds the EXE
+and Rust DLL. This ZIP is not a Windows executable; no ISO or login is included.
+
+The previous live log showed `You queued from another client` when two searches
+overlapped. This diagnostic instead stores Teams locally, connects singles first,
+and sends the Teams request only when actual singles gameplay begins. It does
+not yet establish that the service accepts this different sequence.
+
+## Update your existing GitHub project
+
+Your repository already has the correct 3.7.0 workflow. **Do not edit it again.**
+
+1. Extract this kit. In your existing repository open **Code > parallel-queue**:
+   https://github.com/jacegiddens/preflight-teams-priority/tree/main/parallel-queue
+2. Choose **Add file > Upload files**. Upload ALL FILES INSIDE this kit's
+   `parallel-queue` folder, replacing those files. Commit the upload. Upload the
+   files themselves; do not nest another folder or upload this ZIP.
+3. Open **Actions > Build Windows Teams Priority 3.7.0 test > Run workflow**.
+   Choose `main`, then click the green Run workflow button.
+4. After the run is green, download **Slippi-Teams-Priority-3.7.0-test** from its
+   Artifacts section. Extract the wrapper, then the Windows ZIP inside it into
+   a NEW folder. Follow its included `TESTING.txt` step by step.
+
+A new matching ISO is required. Run the NEW patcher against the ORIGINAL working
+Aitch Preflight v1.1 ISO. Save `Preflight-Jace-Teams-after-Singles-test.iso`.
+Do not reuse Menu Fix 4 or overwrite the original ISO. The executable title must
+include `[Jace Teams-after-Singles test]`. Keep EXE, DLLs and Sys together.
+The normal Launcher installation remains separate. Never upload User/user.json.
+
+## What this test displays
+
+- Yellow ARMED: Teams configured locally; no search has been sent.
+- Yellow CONNECTING: request started, awaiting the server's acceptance.
+- Green SEARCHING: server confirmed the Teams queue.
+- Green READY: all required peer connections established.
+- Red FAILED: displays the actual failure reason.
+
+Status refreshes during singles gameplay through Dolphin's on-screen messages;
+leave Config > Interface > On-Screen Display Messages enabled. Green is evidence
+of acceptance, not proof of a completed four-player handoff.
+
+The original five root menu rows and standard Queue Unranked/Direct/Teams remain.
+The duplicate Play Singles context is removed. Teams starts only after the singles
+game begins. Cancel Teams before searching for a NEW singles opponent in this
+one-game diagnostic; automatic safe pause/resume across new opponents is not
+implemented. Same-opponent singles rematches can retain the Teams search.
+
+The Training description reads:
+
+    Play Unranked or Direct while queuing for doubles! by Jace
+    Originally by Aitch
+
+The original menu artwork is unchanged. Only the caption's loader hook and the
+two game modules are patched by checksum-bound COPY/DATA recipes.
+
+## Server evidence and remaining limits
+
+Official documentation says the matchmaking server source is private:
+https://github.com/project-slippi/slippi-wiki/blob/master/GETTING_STARTED.md
+The client source is public. The earlier live error establishes eviction of an
+earlier same-account search; it does not prove a prohibition on a search during
+an existing peer-to-peer game or establish Slippi's intent toward this feature.
+
+Local checks passed: 97 queue/gating checks, 14 C/host protocol checks, 17 session
+barrier checks, 182 compiled PPC adapter checks, 621 DMA/transfer checks, 5,943
+original-menu navigation checks, native translation-unit compilation, actual DOL
+SIS/caption execution and end-to-end PowerShell synthetic-disc patching. Previous
+Rust independent-client tests also pass against a loopback service; that service
+does not model public account policy. Game SDK/rendering are mocked in PPC menu
+checks. No live Windows/public-service acceptance or four-player handoff is
+claimed. The intermittent UI/CPU stall remains unresolved; this removes the extra
+menu context but is not a verified crash fix.
+
+## Corresponding source and credits
+
+Dolphin base: project-slippi/Ishiiruka at
+`07b2d287a1f074942811d13b3c990fa29401ba7c` (v3.7.0).
+Rust base: project-slippi/slippi-rust-extensions at
+`934f373d3cbcbca9ea3ceb68b53bda875c96abfb`.
+
+The included native and Rust patches reproduce the exact tested source on those
+bases. The unchanged workflow builds the EXE, DLL and matching Sys, then includes
+the source patches and licenses. The kit contains no original game code/assets,
+account file or binary. Aitch created Preflight; this is an independent Jace
+Teams-priority integration. Existing source credits and licenses are retained.
