index 0000000..9e7aba6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Development/SingleInstance/PreflightFindings-2026-11-16.md
@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+# Verified Preflight v1.1 findings — 2026-11-16
+
+Inputs are local user exports, not instructions or editable author source.
+The patch ZIP contains patch.xdelta and patching tools. Exact later exports
+supplied main.dol, filesystem metadata, tm.dat, other.dat and codes.gct.
+
+| File | Bytes | SHA-256 |
+|---|---:|---|
+| main.dol | 4425184 | f604e1399f2dc88e2fbbaa2b3441867ca34d00b99b82e16bee4e4ef108604805 |
+| tm.dat | 95720 | 2a46fda61b0b175c425687bab074b9b06606325bedf3caa5c39e1984007da920 |
+| other.dat | 1304 | 85757d8ede9fef7b69e522fb4a7e38f2f126758f918f6dae14276043c42ca76b |
+| codes.gct | 1312 | 1fdf6c7f11268e39d6bd68124b1b287008869f3e941851eb19b23a34dd54701d |
+
+The supplied disc is GALE01 revision 2, 1,459,978,240 bytes. Its DOL starts at
+124,928. tm.dat has 2,584 bytes of padding before other.dat. Exact module data
+matches all bytes recovered earlier from the xdelta patch.
+
+## Module and scene layout
+
+The DAT files are HSD function archives with root `fns`. Code references use
+loader relocations 1 (ADDR32), 4 (ADDR16_LO), 6 (ADDR16_HA), 10 (REL24) and
+26 (REL32). tm.dat's original code/data length is 0x13A00, with 1,905 code
+relocation records and export 0 at offset 0x9054. other.dat has code/data length
+0x3A8, 34 relocations and export 0 at 0x208. The GCT scene loader loads these
+archives through 0x803D709C. The compiler strings identify GCC/devkitPPC 16.1.0
+and src/tm.c, src/cpu4.c. These are evidence of a compiled PowerPC project,
+not recovery of Aitch's original C source or its build environment.
+
+Scene major 0x1C is training: minors 0 CSS, 1 SSS, 2 practice. Major 8/minor 0
+is the Slippi/VS CSS. other.dat implements L+R and installs a scene-decision
+callback. A practice exit uses the original engine scene functions to return
+to Slippi. Slippi's EXI transfer function is at 0x800055F0. The actual supplied
+DOL sets r2=0x804DF9E0, r13=0x804DB6A0. Online mode is at 0x804D6640;
+0x804D666A is the chose-stage flag, not an invented takeover flag.
+
+## Verified menu structures (module-relative offsets)
+
+Menu rows are 44 bytes: label +0, value label +4, inline value +8,
+press/adjust callbacks +C/+10, state +14, argument +18, context +1C,
+and colors +20/+24/+28. Contexts are 0x80 bytes: next +0, update +4,
+draw +8, row count +C, cursor +10 and row table +14, followed by interpolation
+and style state. Context `next` is an update/draw list, NOT the navigation parent.
+The submenu navigation stack is separate. New contexts must join this list.
+
+- General context 0xC488, 5 rows at 0x9E5C. The apparently empty row at 0x9E88
+  is dynamically populated CPU Actions; it must be retained.
+- Queue context 0xC408, 6 rows at 0x9F38. Ranked/Unranked use 0x4884;
+  Direct uses 0x4588 and context 0xC308; Teams uses 0x4660.
+- Queue callbacks write the shared Slippi mode byte, send selections B5 and
+  search B4, and normally cancel any current foreground with BA.
+- Practice queue polling is 0x8D40 through context callback site 0xC28C.
+  Practice main think 0x4A1C walks the entire context update list every frame,
+  independently of which submenu is open.
+- Practice exit callback 0x4410 uses local flag 0xA1BC to return to major 8.
+  It copies selected character/color from packet 0xC520 and sets chose-stage.
+- other.dat frame callback is 0, scene-exit callback 0xE8 and entry 0x208.
+  L+R requests a normal minor exit, then the exit callback selects training.
+
+## Experimental adapter output
+
+Our adapter changes exported entry callbacks, hooks the existing polling/frame
+callbacks and adds the new menu using existing styles. The native layer parks
+Teams BEFORE existing singles callbacks can send BA, so their cleanup affects
+only the fresh singles context. Native gameplay priority uses fully connected
+Teams peers, rather than server assignment. Real scene behavior still requires
+live testing; simulated imports cannot verify the game's complete control flow.
+
+Patched outputs currently have these hashes:
+
+- tm.dat, 99,172 bytes: e84fa6de1679507a0779c4637ee627e09b7b43b278c0c9f8f5ab21f2895c652e
+- other.dat, 2,996 bytes: 12875c79874e2382ce97d7ce02258098e819272ea53e083ef348fb79da82b0a1
+
+These compiled artifacts and private Ghidra/decompilation work stay local.
+The distributable patch uses checksum-bound COPY/DATA recipes and our source.
+No original game module, DOL, ISO or login file is included in the build kit.
+
+## First live crash and repair
+
+The user confirmed original Preflight works in the custom Windows executable.
+The modified ISO crashed on L+R with an invalid low program counter. The original
+adapter used stack buffers at 0x817DFFD8 (13-byte write) and 0x817DFFC8 (16-byte
+read) in the regression fixture. The real SDK EXIDma routine at 0x80345E60 masks
+both down to 0x817DFFC0, corrupting the frame and losing the request framing.
+Running the old compiled adapter through the real routine reproduces an invalid
+memory fetch. The repair uses a 95-byte private storage region to provide two
+complete runtime-aligned 32-byte DMA cache lines; cleanup BA uses the same safe
+transmit lane. No native protocol or Windows executable change is needed.
+
+The actual supplied GCT relocation routine was also executed against original
+and repaired archives; relocated code matches the analysis decoder byte-for-byte.
+The new test includes the original L+R and scene-exit callbacks, with imported
+SDK/host services mocked. Full game behavior still requires the user's live test.
+
+The larger tm.dat no longer fits its original padding. The patcher retains all
+original occupied ranges and metadata, places it in verified free space starting
+at 4,721,600 in the supplied layout, and updates FST offset/size fields. Other.dat
+fits in place at 4,718,592. Disc length and original DOL/GCT stay unchanged.
+
+## Ordinary Queue menu integration
+
+The original Unranked/Direct/Teams row callback relocation sites are 0x9F70,
+0x9F9C and 0x9FC8. The revised adapter redirects only these buttons: Unranked
+and Direct preserve a waiting Teams search before invoking the ORIGINAL callback
+on its canonical row. Ordinary solo use remains available when no Teams search
+exists. The Teams button uses background-only cancellation when a retained Teams
+session is present, otherwise opens the original team/color interface. Ranked
+and Party callbacks are unchanged. The extra submenu is now an alias rather
+than a requirement to preserve Teams.
+
+The adapter restores the original Teams row's green outline AFTER ordinary
+singles cleanup, based on a fresh native status query. It labels it Queue Teams
+[BG], or displays a red failed state, and clears the label/outline on cancellation.
+These indicators appear in Preflight's Queue menu; no extra online-game HUD was
+added. The tests execute the actual original cleanup/queue functions, including
+their aligned HSD packet transfers, rather than only simulating the callbacks.
+
+## Label revision 3
+
+The user reported the bracketed background abbreviation appeared as "Ge" in the
+real menu. Replace it with plain ASCII words: Teams Background / Teams Ready /
+Teams Failed. The main submenu is now Play Singles. The behavioral logic and
+private native protocol are unchanged. Recent .slp files were found in the root
+replay directory; the apparent missing recordings came from the unchecked monthly
+subfolder preference, not a demonstrated writer failure.
diff --git a/Development/SingleInstance/QueueControlTest.cpp b/Development/SingleInstance/QueueControlTest.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f5580ed
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Development/SingleInstance/QueueControlTest.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,123 @@
+// Copyright 2026 Dolphin Emulator Project
+// Licensed under GPLv2+
+// Refer to the license.txt file included.
+#include "Core/Slippi/SlippiQueueControl.h"
+#include <iostream>
+#include <stdexcept>
+
+using Control = SlippiQueueControl;
+using Op = Control::Op;
+using Result = Control::Result;
+struct FakeBackend : Control::Backend
+{
+  Control::Mode mode = Control::Mode::Teams;
+  bool waiting = false, searching = false;
+  bool busy = false, parkable = true, parked = false, ready = false, failed = false;
+  int foreground_identity = 100, teams_identity = 0;
+  int parks = 0, activations = 0, cancellations = 0;
+  Control::Mode ForegroundMode() const override { return mode; }
+  bool ForegroundBusy() const override { return busy; }
+  bool CanParkTeams() const override { return parkable; }
+  bool HasTeams() const override { return parked; }
+  bool TeamsReady() const override { return ready && !failed; }
+  bool TeamsFailed() const override { return failed; }
+  bool TeamsWaiting() const override { return waiting; }
+  bool TeamsSearching() const override { return searching; }
+  void ParkTeams() override { teams_identity = foreground_identity; foreground_identity = 200; mode = Control::Mode::None; parked = true; ++parks; }
+  void ActivateTeams() override { foreground_identity = teams_identity; teams_identity = 0; parked = false; mode = Control::Mode::Teams; ++activations; }
+  void CancelTeams() override { teams_identity = 0; parked = false; ++cancellations; }
+};
+int checks = 0;
+void Check(bool v, const char* why) { if (!v) throw std::runtime_error(why); ++checks; }
+std::array<std::uint8_t, 12> Request(Op op, std::uint32_t token = 0)
+{
+  return {{'P','F','D','Q',1,static_cast<std::uint8_t>(op),0,0,
+    static_cast<std::uint8_t>(token >> 24),static_cast<std::uint8_t>(token >> 16),
+    static_cast<std::uint8_t>(token >> 8),static_cast<std::uint8_t>(token)}};
+}
+std::uint32_t Token(const Control::Reply& r) { return (std::uint32_t(r[8]) << 24) | (std::uint32_t(r[9]) << 16) | (std::uint32_t(r[10]) << 8) | r[11]; }
+Result Status(const Control::Reply& r) { return static_cast<Result>(r[5]); }
+Control::Reply Call(Control& c, FakeBackend& b, Op op, std::uint32_t token = 0)
+{
+  auto r = Request(op, token); return c.Handle(r.data(), r.size(), b);
+}
+int main()
+{
+  for (int mode : {0,1,2,3,4,255})
+    for (bool connected : {false,true})
+      for (bool ready : {false,true})
+        Check(Control::ShouldYieldToTeams(static_cast<Control::Mode>(mode), connected, ready) ==
+              ((mode == 1 || mode == 2) && connected && ready),
+              "only connected Direct/Unranked yield to connected Teams");
+  for (auto mode : {Control::Mode::Ranked, Control::Mode::Unranked, Control::Mode::Direct,
+                    Control::Mode::Teams, Control::Mode::None})
+    for (bool connected : {false,true})
+      for (bool started : {false,true})
+        Check(Control::CanStartDeferred(mode,connected,started) ==
+              ((mode==Control::Mode::Unranked || mode==Control::Mode::Direct) && connected && started),
+              "deferred search requires an actual connected singles game; never Ranked/Teams");
+  { Control staged; FakeBackend state; state.parked=true; staged.TeamsChanged();
+    state.waiting=true;
+    auto armed=Call(staged,state,Op::Status);
+    Check(armed[6]==9 && Token(armed)!=0,"locally armed queue has a cancellation token and only waiting flag");
+    state.waiting=false;
+    Check(Call(staged,state,Op::Status)[6]==1,"connecting is not reported as server-confirmed searching");
+    state.searching=true;
+    Check(Call(staged,state,Op::Status)[6]==17,"searching flag requires explicit confirmation");
+    state.failed=true;
+    Check(Call(staged,state,Op::Status)[6]==5,"failure suppresses stale searching state");
+    auto token=Token(armed); staged.TeamsChanged();
+    Check(Status(Call(staged,state,Op::CancelTeams,token))==Result::StaleGeneration,"old UI event cannot cancel a new configuration");
+  }
+  Control c; FakeBackend b;
+  auto r = Call(c,b,Op::Capabilities);
+  Check(r[0]=='P' && r[3]=='Q' && r[4]==1 && r[15]==31, "explicit version/capability reply");
+  Check(b.parks==0 && b.activations==0 && b.cancellations==0, "discovery does not mutate sessions");
+  for (std::size_t size = 0; size < 20; ++size)
+  {
+    if (size==12) continue;
+    auto q=Request(Op::ParkTeams);
+    Check(Status(c.Handle(q.data(),size,b))==Result::Malformed, "bad length rejected before access");
+  }
+  Check(Status(c.Handle(nullptr,12,b))==Result::Malformed, "null request rejected");
+  for (int index : {0,1,2,3,6,7})
+  {
+    auto q=Request(Op::ParkTeams);q[index]^=32;
+    Check(Status(c.Handle(q.data(),q.size(),b))==Result::Malformed, "signature/reserved fields checked");
+  }
+  auto q=Request(Op::ParkTeams);q[4]=2;
+  Check(Status(c.Handle(q.data(),q.size(),b))==Result::UnsupportedVersion, "version mismatch cannot park");
+  q=Request(Op::ParkTeams);q[5]=255;
+  Check(Status(c.Handle(q.data(),q.size(),b))==Result::UnsupportedOperation, "unknown operation rejected");
+  Check(b.parks==0, "invalid packets never change foreground ownership");
+  b.mode=Control::Mode::Ranked;
+  Check(Status(Call(c,b,Op::ParkTeams))==Result::WrongMode, "Ranked cannot become background search");
+  b.mode=Control::Mode::Unranked;
+  Check(Status(Call(c,b,Op::ParkTeams))==Result::WrongMode, "only Teams can be parked");
+  b.mode=Control::Mode::Teams;b.parkable=false;
+  Check(Status(Call(c,b,Op::ParkTeams))==Result::Busy, "active/unsafe Teams session cannot park");
+  b.parkable=true;
+  Check(Status(Call(c,b,Op::ParkTeams,7))==Result::StaleGeneration, "park must start without a token");
+  r=Call(c,b,Op::ParkTeams);auto generation=Token(r);
+  Check(Status(r)==Result::Ok && generation!=0 && (r[6]&1), "Teams search retained with generation");
+  Check(b.foreground_identity==200 && b.teams_identity==100 && b.parks==1, "foreground and standby keep distinct identities");
+  Check(Status(Call(c,b,Op::ParkTeams))==Result::AlreadyParked && b.parks==1, "duplicate park does not lose Teams");
+  Check(Status(Call(c,b,Op::ActivateTeams,0))==Result::StaleGeneration, "zero token cannot activate");
+  Check(Status(Call(c,b,Op::CancelTeams,generation+1))==Result::StaleGeneration && b.parked, "stale cancellation preserves current Teams");
+  Check(Status(Call(c,b,Op::ActivateTeams,generation))==Result::NotReady, "assignment alone cannot take over");
+  b.mode=Control::Mode::Direct;b.busy=true;b.ready=true;
+  Check(Status(Call(c,b,Op::ActivateTeams,generation))==Result::Busy && b.activations==0, "live singles must exit before Teams activation");
+  r=Call(c,b,Op::Status);
+  Check((r[6]&3)==3 && b.mode==Control::Mode::Direct, "ready status does not silently swap live game");
+  b.busy=false;r=Call(c,b,Op::ActivateTeams,generation);
+  Check(Status(r)==Result::Ok && b.foreground_identity==100 && b.mode==Control::Mode::Teams && !b.parked, "explicit safe activation restores same Teams identity");
+  Check(Status(Call(c,b,Op::ActivateTeams,generation))==Result::StaleGeneration && b.activations==1, "late singles event cannot reactivate old generation");
+  b.foreground_identity=300;r=Call(c,b,Op::ParkTeams);generation=Token(r);
+  b.mode=Control::Mode::Unranked;b.busy=true;
+  Check(Status(Call(c,b,Op::CancelTeams,generation))==Result::Ok && b.foreground_identity==200 && b.mode==Control::Mode::Unranked, "cancel background leaves live singles intact");
+  Check(Status(Call(c,b,Op::ActivateTeams,Token(Call(c,b,Op::Status))))==Result::NoTeams, "empty standby cannot activate");
+  b.mode=Control::Mode::Teams;Call(c,b,Op::ParkTeams);b.failed=true;b.ready=true;
+  r=Call(c,b,Op::Status);
+  Check((r[6]&4)!=0 && (r[6]&2)==0, "failed connection cannot be reported ready");
+  std::cout << checks << " queue-control protocol/lifecycle checks passed. No online connection or game was run.\n";
+}
