+# Singles while Teams searches — one Dolphin instance
+
+Experimental implementation, ported 2026-11-17. Target: Windows 11, Slippi 3.7.0,
+Preflight v1.1, one render window and the original GameCube adapter input path.
+There is no desktop switching helper in this implementation.
+
+## Implemented source and compiled game adapter
+
+- EXI owns a parked Teams matchmaking context and a separate foreground context.
+  Character/color/team/code/stages remain attached to the parked Teams search.
+- A private versioned EXI command (E6, PFDQ version 1) discovers capabilities,
+  parks, queries, activates and cancels Teams. Generation tokens reject stale
+  events. Stock Slippi does not expose the new menu.
+- The active netplay marker uses atomic identity ownership. A standby client's
+  construction/destruction cannot take over or clear another client's marker.
+- Successful Teams peer connections make an active Direct/Unranked game follow
+  the normal disconnect path. Ranked and Teams never yield through this policy.
+- Activation waits for ordinary foreground cleanup, online game end, report
+  submission and asynchronous replay writes. Local practice replay writes do
+  not prevent parking. Replay metadata is snapshotted before queue changes.
+- Rust opaque-device calls share a per-device gate; cleanup workers are joined
+  before the Rust device/user or ENet are destroyed. Concurrent contexts do not
+  bind the same configured netplay port.
+- Compiled PowerPC adapters intercept the ORIGINAL Queue Unranked and Queue
+  Direct buttons to retain a waiting Teams session. Teams Background stays green
+  from the emulator's background status alongside the active singles option;
+  failed Teams turns red. Clicking Teams while Background is shown cancels only that
+  background session. The extra Play Singles submenu remains a compatible alias
+  with a background-cancel option. They retain the original L+R, direct-code entry,
+  menu rendering and scene callbacks. The new submenu joins the existing menu
+  update/draw chain. The five original root rows remain, including CPU Actions.
+- A ready Teams session leaves practice or restarts the singles CSS in Teams
+  mode, performs normal cleanup, then requests activation. Busy report/replay
+  state is retried without repeatedly cancelling foreground state. Parked Teams
+  selections remain protected through its first game setup.
+
+The first test queues Teams BEFORE entering Unranked. Starting a Teams search
+from inside an already-running singles game is not implemented. The singles
+match ends; it cannot be resumed later. There is no automatic requeue or failed
+handoff recovery yet. Native Phob/Lossless access is retained by using one
+Dolphin; actual hardware timing and live matchmaking remain unverified.
+
+## Validation performed here
+
+- 116 standalone C/C++ checks: active ownership, versioned protocol/generations,
+  priority modes, gameplay/report/replay barriers, serialized Rust access, and
+  the C game client communicating with the real C++ protocol parser.
+- 180 checks executing the compiled big-endian PowerPC adapters under Unicorn
+  with mocked game/EXI services. These check relocated menu registration,
+  stock-host refusal, parking, Unranked/Direct dispatch, cancellation, readiness,
+  CSS restart, busy retries, Teams activation and preserved EABI stack/GPRs.
+- Five changed native translation units compiled against actual Slippi headers
+  to Linux objects. This is not a linked Dolphin application or a Windows build.
+- 657 expanded checks run the upstream Slippi EXI transfer code and the supplied
+  DOL's EXIDma instructions with mocked host/SDK services, across eight module
+  alignments and two stack alignments. The old code reproduces an invalid
+  memory fetch. The fixed code keeps all DMA off the stack. Additional cases
+  execute Preflight's real original L+R/entry/exit callbacks. The expanded queue
+  cases also execute the original Unranked, Direct, Teams and cancellation
+  handlers to check that their ordinary cleanup preserves the background and
+  that both queue outlines accurately reflect the independent native states.
+- The PowerShell ISO patcher passed exact synthetic-disc byte comparison,
+  preservation of the original, existing-output refusal, altered-module
+  rejection and insufficient-free-space rejection. Its successful output differs
+  only in the two patched modules and their FST offset/size fields.
+
+The Windows build and isolated component tests succeeded in GitHub run
+https://github.com/jacegiddens/preflight-teams-priority/actions/runs/43989092819.
+The user confirmed original Preflight opens in that executable, but the first
+modified ISO crashed during L+R. Investigation found the game SDK masks DMA
+buffer addresses to 32-byte boundaries; the new request buffers were unaligned
+stack arrays. The repair gives transmit, reply and cleanup commands dedicated,
+runtime-aligned complete cache lines. The EXI protocol/native binary is unchanged.
+
+A full live Teams handoff remains unverified. The new DMA tests execute actual
+transfer/address-mask instructions but do not emulate the whole game's renderer,
+SDK, cache or matchmaking server. The user confirmed the alignment repair opens Preflight and its pause menu.
+They then used the ordinary Queue menu, whose original buttons still replaced
+Teams because only the extra submenu had been connected. The next revision
+intercepts those ordinary buttons and displays independent background status;
+its live queue/outline/handoff behavior still requires verification.
+
+## Supported input and reconstruction
+
+Base emulator: project-slippi/Ishiiruka tag v3.6.4,
+commit e7711b104b339a99385f2bb12b472d46140a7bc7.
+The original Preflight is by Aitch. Its supplied patch and compiled modules are
+not an editable source release. No upstream fork/PR has been published here.
+
+Exact input hashes and structural findings are in PreflightFindings-2026-11-16.md.
+Tools/build_preflight_modules.py rebuilds the HSD function archives from exact
+originals and our relocatable ELF32 PowerPC adapters. It keeps original code and
+global offsets, clones the root rows and a menu context, appends our code, and
+updates relevant relocations and export 0. It refuses unknown originals.
+Analysis base 0x81000000 is arbitrary, never a runtime patch address.
+
+The repaired tm.dat is 99,172 bytes (+3,452); the original slot has only 2,584
+bytes of spare padding. The updated patcher reserves metadata and every original
+file range, prefers in-place placement where safe, otherwise places the enlarged
+module in a verified gap and updates its FST offset and size. With the supplied
+filesystem, tm.dat moves to disc offset 4,721,600. Other.dat becomes 2,996 bytes
+and remains at 4,718,592. main.dol and codes.gct remain unchanged.
+Tools/make_module_delta.py packages COPY/DATA recipes with SHA-256 checks;
+Tools/Patch-Preflight.ps1 uses those recipes to create a NEW ISO, never overwriting
+an existing output or the original. No original DOL/DAT or ISO is distributed.
+
+## Build and first live test
+
+BuildKit contains the GitHub Windows build template and first-test instructions.
+The generated upload kit holds a source patch against the pinned upstream and
+our ISO patch recipe, without user credentials or game exports. The workflow
+checks isolated components on Windows, builds the ordinary WX executable and
+packages its dependencies with the ISO patcher. Original settings are copied by
+the user locally into the test build's portable User folder once.
+
+Live acceptance criteria are still open:
+
+1. Both real matchmaking contexts remain alive with the same account.
+2. Singles selection/disconnection preserves the correct Teams session/ticket.
+3. Fully connected Teams peers trigger one takeover; failed assignments do not.
+4. A real game ends, reports and closes its replay before the correct Teams lobby.
+5. Saved Teams character/color/team and native Phob inputs survive that transition.
+6. Stopping/cancelling/relaunching cleans up the right resources without stalls.
+
+## Replay and Launcher findings
+
+The user found recent .slp files directly in the configured replay directory.
+Recording is working; monthly subfolders were unchecked in the independent
+portable configuration. Enable that option to match the usual layout. Existing
+root files are not moved automatically. No replay-writer change was made for
+this issue. The custom build retains ordinary .slp output.
+
+This feature requires BOTH the modified emulator (second matchmaking context,
+private control command and safe handoff) and game adapter (menus/transitions).
+Launching only the ISO with an unmodified emulator does not add that host support.
+Launcher source inspected at project-slippi/slippi-launcher commit
+45dd53630b38f647dda88943374d61e31f5c1c15 manages its own executable in the netplay
+installation directory; the inspected settings do not include a custom executable
+selector. Its Play button could use the custom binary only after a deliberate
+installation/integration. Its updater may replace that managed copy. No Launcher
+installation or settings were changed in this workspace. The normal Launcher can
+still browse/play standard online-match replays written to its configured folder.
+
+## Cancellation menu update 4 and unresolved live report
+
+The user confirmed that selecting an active Direct search again clears its green
+outline. They also reported an earlier disappearance of the practice menus,
+possibly after cancelling a queue, and a CPU::PauseAndLock synchronization warning;
+neither happened during their latest solo test. The exact trigger remains unknown.
+That warning means the host waited ten seconds for the CPU to become idle; it does
+not establish which operation blocked the CPU.
+
+The Cancel Teams submenu used a right-aligned "Cancelled" value that overlapped
+its long action label. It now leaves the value empty both after cancellation and
+when no Teams search exists; clearing the ordinary Teams outline remains the
+visible confirmation. Compiled adapter tests and tests using the original queue
+handlers check that this action preserves singles and the menu pointers and does
+not request a scene exit. These are isolated tests, not a full game/render test.
+This update does not change native threading or claim to fix the warning or the
+reported menu disappearance. A reproducible trigger or a thread trace is still
+needed for that investigation. Live four-player takeover remains unverified.
+
+Follow-up live report: the user confirmed that cancelling Teams clears only its
+outline while Direct stays green. They also reported another earlier crash after
+repeated Cancel Teams presses and then opening the Teams menu, probably on
+menu-fix-4.iso. Retrying that sequence and a normal Teams cancellation did not
+reproduce the crash. Independent cancellation is now supported by live evidence
+in both directions; intermittent menu disappearance/crashing remains open.
+
+Tools/test_ppc_menus.py adds a focused regression for that sequence. It executes
+the original practice menu-stack transitions, controller-input aggregation and
+context-update instructions, as well as the compiled adapters and real EXI/DMA
+instructions. Twenty cycles with ten cancellation presses each, reopening Teams
+colors and returning to the root, passed 2,640 checks. Physics is skipped after
+the update loop; rendering, SDK and matchmaking services are mocked. This did
+not reproduce or diagnose the Windows crash and is not a substitute for a full
+emulator thread trace. No runtime code or new player build changed in this step.
+
+## Slippi 3.7.0 migration
+
+Base: Ishiiruka `07b2d287a1f074942811d13b3c990fa29401ba7c`, with its Rust submodule
+`934f373d3cbcbca9ea3ceb68b53bda875c96abfb`. The merge retains upstream 3.7.0
+matchmaking, input suggestions, replay additions and other changes; network
+version remains the real 3.7.0. No version spoofing or server check bypass is used.
+
+The new upstream Rust matchmaking singleton cancels its previous session on
+start. Each C++ matchmaking object instead owns a separate independent Rust
+client handle sharing identity/version/endpoint but no ticket/worker/result.
+See Rust/slippi-rust-3.7.0.patch and Rust/README.md for corresponding source and
+tests. The Windows workflow applies that patch to the pinned published submodule;
+the Dolphin gitlink itself stays on the official commit.
+
+Only an explicitly activated netplay client becomes the adapter input-suggestion
+sink. Late remote pads, suggestions and selection-triggered tracker resets are
+also gated by active identity under the sink mutex. This prevents a waiting or
+retiring connection from changing the active game's process-wide tracker.
+
+All nine Rust matchmaking unit tests passed, including loopback WebSocket
+cancellation in both directions with one synthetic account identity. Cargo check,
+FFI test-target linking (no unit tests in that target), and a Linux shared-library
+build passed; all seven new exported functions were verified. All five changed
+native translation units compiled against 3.7.0 headers, and the 116 standalone
+C/C++ checks passed. The compiled game adapter checks (180) and original menu
+navigation checks (2,640) passed with the unchanged Menu Fix 4 objects. The
+upstream EXI bootloader blob is identical between 3.6.4 and 3.7.0. The B3 match-state
+prefix read by Preflight is retained; 3.7.0's new fields are appended. The new
+upstream B0 payload size (27) and Sys game assets are retained in the new build.
+
+The game-side private protocol and patched DAT module bytes are unchanged, so
+the current Menu Fix 4 ISO can be selected in the new build. The first live check
+must still be opening Preflight and its pause menu before queueing, because the
+full 3.7.0 runtime/assets were not emulated here. Windows build execution, public
+service acceptance of both same-account searches, four-player takeover and native
+hardware timing still require live testing. The earlier intermittent UI/CPU stall
+is not claimed fixed by this migration. The old 3.6.4 build remains separately
+preserved. See BuildKit/README.md for the existing-repository Windows build step.
+
+## Live 3.7.0 result: same-account search rejected
+
+The user's Windows build succeeded, Preflight menus opened, and an actual
+Unranked connection/game ran. Their supplied Slippi Online/Rust Online log then
+established why the retained Teams row turned red. The relevant elapsed-log
+sequence (account IDs, ticket IDs and addresses omitted) was:
+
+- 02:00.887: first search started; its ticket was accepted at 02:01.198.
+- 02:03.621: Teams was parked and the foreground search started.
+- 02:04.070: Rust logged `You queued from another client`.
+- 02:04.072: the newer ticket was accepted.
+- 02:04.146: the C++ matchmaking path received that server error.
+- 02:04.305 onward: Unranked matched/connected; game input began at 02:08.226.
+
+Thus Teams failed when the second search started, before the Unranked game,
+although the user noticed the red menu row after returning to practice. This
+is observed live service eviction of the earlier same-account search; it is not
+evidence of a game-end cleanup failure or a timeout in this trace. The error
+indicator correctly stopped describing that search as healthy.
+
+The independent Rust handles and loopback tests establish client-side isolation,
+but the mock server did not enforce this live account/session policy. The
+same-account design cannot be considered functional on the 3.7.0 service from
+these results. Further identical matchmaking tests are unnecessary. A supported
+multi-search service flow, or a design using separately authenticated legitimate
+accounts that the service accepts, needs investigation before another live build
+is warranted. No server checks or account identities have been bypassed.
+The earlier intermittent UI/CPU-stall report remains a separate unresolved issue.
+
+## Current deferred-search diagnostic source
+
+See Research/Server-and-Deferred-Test.md for the official public-source findings,
+new state flags, post-connection gate and validation. Teams is now configured
+locally and only requested after actual singles gameplay begins. Green means
+server-confirmed queued status, not merely an allocated local object. The
+original five-row menu is restored and the duplicate Play Singles context removed.
+The new window title identifies this diagnostic, and a new matching ISO is
+required; the earlier Menu Fix 4 ISO is not this test. Source and compiled game modules are prepared. The requested English caption
+and “Originally by Aitch” credit are implemented in the original loader's SIS hook;
+MnMaAll.usd remains untouched. The updated ISO recipe patches the two game modules
+and only that loader caption. Local PPC/SIS and end-to-end patcher checks passed.
+The Windows source/update kit uses the existing 3.7.0 GitHub workflow. Windows CI
+and the public-service test still need to run; no live success is claimed.
