+# Public server research and the deferred Teams diagnostic
+
+Official Slippi documentation was checked at:
+https://github.com/project-slippi/slippi-wiki/blob/master/GETTING_STARTED.md
+
+It states: "The source code for the matchmaking server is in a private repository
+and is not currently planned to be open sourced."
+The official organization's public repositories were also enumerated; no matching
+server implementation was found. A public web search for the exact rejection
+message did not find published server code or a policy explaining that rule.
+The 3.7.0 Rust client and protocol are public; the live user's log establishes the
+specific earlier-search eviction. These findings do not establish developer intent
+or whether the service accepts one search during an established peer-to-peer game.
+
+## Implemented diagnostic source
+
+1. Queue Teams in the original Preflight menu saves its selections/code locally.
+   It does NOT send a Teams ticket. HasTeams + Waiting flags show yellow Armed.
+2. Original Queue Unranked / Queue Direct starts the foreground search normally.
+3. Only an actual active singles game with a connected peer, positive game frame,
+   and no local-leave request starts the saved Teams matchmaking object, once.
+4. HasTeams alone means Connecting (yellow). Only Rust RUST_MM_QUEUED confirmation
+   makes TeamsSearching true (green). Ready requires every expected peer connected;
+   errors are red with their reason. A typed native OSD status is refreshed during
+   gameplay and EXI status requests. It requires Dolphin's usual OSD setting enabled.
+5. The existing fully-connected handoff/report/replay barrier is retained. After
+   activation the OSD says MATCH CONNECTED, rather than incorrectly saying off.
+6. A new singles search while a Teams request has already started is blocked with
+   an explicit instruction to cancel Teams first. This one-game diagnostic does
+   not pretend to implement automatic safe pause/resume/requeue across new opponents.
+7. Legacy parking cannot be invoked in this test. Its capability bit identifies
+   the new sequential test; the new game adapter rejects an old host's capability
+   response. An UPDATED ISO and native executable must be used together.
+
+The duplicate Play Singles submenu and its extra context/relocated root array are
+removed. The original five root entries and normal Queue buttons remain. Clicking
+Armed/Searching/Failed Teams cancels only its configuration/search.
+
+The intended bottom caption is:
+Play Unranked or Direct while queuing for doubles! by Jace
+Originally by Aitch
+
+The caption is implemented as a two-line encoded SIS string in the original
+codes.gct Training-caption C2 hook at 0x803A63A4. Inspecting the supplied English
+MnMaAll.usd archive ruled that artwork out; it remains unchanged. Only this one
+caption hook grows, with recalculated branch distances and Gecko payload length.
+Every other loader-code byte remains unchanged. Native SIS copy, six PPC selector
+paths and actual font-margin checks passed. The 96/256 scale gives two 12-unit
+lines, narrower than the original caption; live rendering still needs checking.
+The public kit contains a checksum-bound COPY/DATA recipe, never original game
+modules, loader files or font artwork. Existing Aitch/source credits remain.
+
+The PowerShell patcher now applies all three recipes (tm.dat, other.dat,
+codes.gct), reserves all other disc ranges, verifies hashes and saves a new ISO.
+A synthetic-disc end-to-end run passed exact-output/original-preservation,
+existing-output refusal, altered-module/loader rejection and no-space rejection.
+
+Validation so far: 97 host queue/gating checks, 14 C/host protocol checks, 17
+session-barrier checks, 182 compiled PPC hook checks, 621 real transfer/DMA checks,
+and 5,943 original-menu-navigation checks, plus native translation-unit compilation.
+Game SDK/rendering and server services are mocked in the PPC tests. The diagnostic
+has NOT run in Windows or against public matchmaking, and no crash fix is claimed.
