+# Rust matchmaking changes for Slippi 3.7.0
+
+Apply `slippi-rust-3.7.0.patch` inside the official Rust submodule at commit
+`934f373d3cbcbca9ea3ceb68b53bda875c96abfb`. The Dolphin gitlink remains pinned to
+that published upstream commit; the Windows workflow applies this separate patch.
+The generated FFI header is included and regenerated by Cargo's normal build.
+
+Each C++ matchmaking context now owns an independent Rust client handle. It shares
+the account identity, version and endpoint, but not its ticket, result, worker or
+cancellation flag. The original single-client FFI remains available. A context
+joins its C++ worker before destroying its Rust handle; cancelling or destroying a
+standby client therefore cannot cancel the active client's session.
+
+Two local-only tests cover isolated cancellation/drop/stale IDs and two real
+WebSocket connections to a loopback mock service, using the same synthetic user.
+The WebSocket test exercises cancellation in both directions and confirms that
+the surviving queue can still receive its result. No real account or production
+matchmaking request is used. All nine matchmaking crate unit tests passed locally.
+Cargo check and a Linux shared-library build passed; all seven new symbols were
+verified in the linked library. This does not establish Windows or public-service
+compatibility; the Windows workflow and a live Teams test remain required.
+
+Upstream source/license: https://github.com/project-slippi/slippi-rust-extensions/tree/934f373d3cbcbca9ea3ceb68b53bda875c96abfb
